   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🌊 Geospatial Intelligence & Agentic AI for Disaster Risk Reduction\n",
    "## A Comprehensive El Niño Early Warning Strategy for Garissa County (2026)\n",
    "\n",
    "This interactive notebook synthesizes hydrometeorological modeling, remote sensing, and spatial analytics to build a high-fidelity risk narrative for Garissa County ahead of the predicted late-2026 El Niño event."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1. The Macro Context: Historical Baseline (April 2024)\n",
    "The 2024 flood extents (captured by UNOSAT) serve as our empirical baseline of vulnerability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import geopandas as gpd\n",
    "import folium\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load Garissa County Boundary\n",
    "county = gpd.read_file('garissa_county.shp')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load 2024 UNOSAT Flood Extents\n",
    "flood_2024 = gpd.read_file('flood_extents.shp')\n",
    "if flood_2024.crs != 'EPSG:4326':\n",
    "    flood_2024 = flood_2024.to_crs('EPSG:4326')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Initialize map centered on Garissa\n",
    "m = folium.Map(location=[-0.4532, 39.6461], zoom_start=8, tiles='CartoDB positron')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add County Boundary\n",
    "folium.GeoJson(county, style_function=lambda x: {'color': 'black', 'fillColor': 'transparent', 'weight': 2}, name=\"Garissa Boundary\").add_to(m)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add Historical Floods\n",
    "folium.GeoJson(flood_2024, style_function=lambda x: {'color': 'blue', 'fillColor': 'blue', 'weight': 1, 'fillOpacity': 0.5}, name=\"2024 Floods (UNOSAT)\").add_to(m)\n",
    "\n",
    "folium.LayerControl().add_to(m)\n",
    "m"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. Identifying At-Risk Infrastructure (2026 Projection)\n",
    "By applying geoprocessing buffers (simulating a Super El Niño) to the baseline geometry, we've identified specific schools, health facilities, and boreholes at risk. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "def get_color(risk):\n",
    "    if risk == 'High Risk': return 'red'\n",
    "    if risk == 'Medium Risk': return 'orange'\n",
    "    if risk == 'Low Risk': return 'yellow'\n",
    "    return 'green'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load assessed data\n",
    "schools = gpd.read_file('OUTPUT/garissa_schools_Risk_Assessed.geojson')\n",
    "health = gpd.read_file('OUTPUT/garissa_health_facilities_Risk_Assessed.geojson')\n",
    "boreholes = gpd.read_file('OUTPUT/Cleaned_Garissa_Boreholes_Risk_Assessed.geojson')\n",
    "\n",
    "risk_map = folium.Map(location=[-0.4532, 39.6461], zoom_start=9, tiles='CartoDB dark_matter')\n",
    "folium.GeoJson(flood_2024, style_function=lambda x: {'color': '#1f78b4', 'weight': 0.5, 'fillOpacity': 0.3}, name=\"Flood Baseline\").add_to(risk_map)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add points with risk colors\n",
    "for idx, row in health.iterrows():\n",
    "    folium.CircleMarker(location=[row.geometry.y, row.geometry.x], radius=4,\n",
    "                        popup=f\"Health Facility Risk: {row.get('Risk_Level', 'Unknown')}\",\n",
    "                        color=get_color(row.get('Risk_Level', 'Safe')), fill=True).add_to(risk_map)\n",
    "                        \n",
    "risk_map"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Logistical Mitigation Strategy\n",
    "- **June - September 2026**: Pre-position medical supplies and cholera kits at `Safe` health facilities.\n",
    "- Establish evacuation routes from `High Risk` schools toward elevated topography.\n",
    "- Reinforce `Low Risk` boreholes as they will be the primary safe water source if closer wells are contaminated."
   ]
  }
